{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792695484,"nonce":"rY9Hjss4+5V4dawFIf1GKZj4Y1c=","message":"RayDE new-tab investigation on 2026-10-22:\n\nThe pre-fix release probe opened Welcome, ImagePreview, ExplorerOutline, CommandCenter and LspClient in one server. Every subsequent page reported reused=true. The slow ImagePreview analysis still compiled 202 newly reached imports; LspClient compiled zero. Warm Welcome reopen requests took 132–133 ms. Logs: /tmp/rayzor-lsp-new-tabs-before.log and /tmp/rayzor-lsp-cache-new-tabs-before-stderr.log. These are baseline measurements, not timings of the new patch.\n\nOpening a source already lowered as an import still called lower_to_tast, repeating import discovery and compiler hooks. It also added that source to user_files, consuming the root-page allowance. A graph at its root-page limit could be rejected even when the requested dependency was already present.\n\nThe new path checks canonical compiled-file identity and indexes an existing typed dependency directly. It keeps source/configuration and macro-resource validation, then persists the resulting editor answers through the existing BLADE path. Already typed dependencies remain eligible at the graph limit. New root files continue sharing the existing graph while it can be extended.\n\nCoverage includes stable graph/source identity without another driver pass, reuse at the root-page limit, and a protocol test opening a macro-generated dependency as a new tab then restoring its generated type from BLADE after restart without rerunning its build macro. Validation results will follow.","files":null}]}